        ActionMenuBox["\"Help\"", {"\"Tips\"" :> MessageDialog[
            Column[{
              TextCell[
               DisplayForm[
               "1. Set the number of lattices by the slider.\n2. Input the \
coordinates of 2D basis vectors for each lattice. The length of the vector is \
1 by default.\n3. Set sub-unit-cell atoms and corresponding scattering \
factors in \
\"\!\(\*StyleBox[\"Structure\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\" \
\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\"factors\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\)\"\
 for each lattice.\n4. Click \
\"\!\(\*StyleBox[\"Reciprocal\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\" \
\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\"lattices\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\)\
\" in the bottom panel, and the 2D reciprocal space will be updated.\n5. \
Click \"\!\(\*StyleBox[\"RHEED\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\" \
\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\)\!\(\*StyleBox[\"Simulation\",FontWeight->\"Bold\"]\
\)\" button. A new dialog window will pop up showing the simulated RHEED \
pattern, where several parameters can be customized. The simulation is auto \
updated."], "Text", TextAlignment -> Left, TextJustification -> 1]}], 
            WindowTitle -> "Tips", WindowSize -> {500, All}], 
          "\"Scattering factors\"" :> MessageDialog[
            Column[{
              Hyperlink[
              "J. M. Cowley, Scattering factors for the diffraction of \
